From: djsaunde <1245942+djsaunde@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:18:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] fast: flip depth read-back rows when the game draws into
 the window

GetPixelDepth takes top-down game coordinates. A game framebuffer is drawn
upside down, so its rows already run top-down, but when there is no game
framebuffer (mRendersToFb false: a port without the LUS GUI, which draws
straight into the window) the window's rows run bottom-up and the lookup
read the vertically mirrored pixel. Flip y in that case.

Found by the 1080 port's golden tests (patch 3's depth read-back on the
split-screen scene read the bottom window's depth for the top window).
---
 src/fast/interpreter.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
index a410c20..f7a0b54 100644
--- a/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
+++ b/src/fast/interpreter.cpp
@@ -5475,6 +5475,10 @@ void Interpreter::AdjustPixelDepthCoordinates(float& x, float& y) {
     x = x * RATIO_X(mActiveFrameBuffer, mCurDimensions) -
         (mNativeDimensions.width * RATIO_X(mActiveFrameBuffer, mCurDimensions) - mCurDimensions.width) / 2;
     y *= RATIO_Y(mActiveFrameBuffer, mCurDimensions);
+    if (!mRendersToFb) {
+        // the game drew straight into the window, whose rows run bottom-up (game framebuffers are drawn flipped)
+        y = mGameWindowViewport.height - 1 - y;
+    }
     if (!mRendersToFb || (mMsaaLevel > 1 && mCurDimensions.width == mGameWindowViewport.width &&
                           mCurDimensions.height == mGameWindowViewport.height)) {
         x += mGameWindowViewport.x;
